  - extended rhetorical graph
abstract: >
  The RhetConnect Corpus v1.0 is the first publicly available corpus of
  multimedia educational documents annotated with cross-media rhetorical
  structure following the Extended Rhetorical Graph (ERG) formalism. It
  comprises 40 documents (559 Elementary Simple Units, 114 Elementary
  Composite Units, 396 rhetorical relations) spanning 10 academic domains,
  sourced from CK-12 Foundation open educational resources and original
  constructed documents. Inter-annotator agreement on relation labels
  reached Cohen's kappa = 0.82. The corpus was built to empirically
  validate the RhetConnect algorithm for coherence-preserving multimedia
  document adaptation.
